    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier grade of 83.29. Facing Sean Burke, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and favorable park factors, cementing his status as the cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive strategy. **Jacob Wilson** also provides significant value at 74.07, leveraging a prime matchup against Eric Lauer\u2019s 4.69 xERA; his situational boost from an expected #5 spot in the order, combined with a strong SP skill metric, makes him an essential start. While **Cole Carrigg** (69.11) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.06) both carry high scores, **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing due to his high stolen base potential against Eduardo Rodriguez, who is notoriously susceptible to the running game.\n\nThe decision to exclude **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (50.42) from the starting lineup was the day's tightest margin. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** projected well, his negative platoon split against the tough southpaw Ranger Suarez outweighed his favorable spot in the batting order. We are proceeding with caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors like **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci**; if their projected spots in the order fluctuate downward, their efficiency scores will need to be re-evaluated. **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest test of our starters against Shota Imanaga; despite a 5% boost from wind-aided conditions, his platoon disadvantage remains a point of concern. We will continue to monitor the weather and official lineups, but as it stands, the combination of speed from **Cole Carrigg** and **Heliot Ramos** combined with the power of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.08) creates a balanced, high-efficiency attack for the Waves.",
